 "response": {
  "text": "If your budget is **₹2,000**, I’d prioritize these brands for men in India:\n\n### [Levi's 505 Straight Fit Men Mid Rise Jeans]()\n*₹1,504*\n\n### [Pepe Jeans Men Blue Mid Rise Straight Fit Jeans]()\n*₹1,401.65*\n\n### [Wrangler Men's Millard Straight Fit Mid-Rise Jeans]()\n*₹1,500*\n\n### [Lee Men's Travis Slim Fit Jeans]()\n*₹1,700*\n\n### [The Roadster Life Co. Men's Regular Fit Jeans]()\n*₹735*\n\n### My ranking\n\n1. **Levi's — best overall** ⭐  \n   If you find a Levi's 505/513/512 around ₹1,500–₹2,000, I'd buy it. Levi's currently has several men's styles below ₹2,000 on its India store, including the 513 at ₹1,679 and 505 at ₹1,975. [levi.in](https://levi.in/collections/men-jeans?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n2. **Pepe Jeans — best value**  \n   Excellent choice when discounted. Current Pepe listings include straight-fit jeans around **₹1,499**, with some at ₹1,999. [www.pepejeans.in](https://www.pepejeans.in/men/jeans?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n3. **Wrangler — best for comfort/regular fit**  \n   A particularly good choice if you don't like skinny jeans. There's currently a Millard straight-fit option around ₹1,500. \n\n4. **Lee — good for comfortable everyday wear**  \n   Worth considering if you find a discounted pair around ₹1,500–₹1,800.\n\n5. **Roadster — best budget option**  \n   If you want to spend only ₹700–₹1,200, Roadster offers very good value; current Myntra listings have regular/straight fits below ₹1,000. [www.myntra.com](https://www.myntra.com/men-jeans?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n**If it were my ₹2,000:** I'd get **Levi's first**, **Pepe second**, and **Wrangler third**.\n\nFor maximum versatility, choose **dark blue or medium blue, straight/slim-straight fit**, rather than heavily distressed or very skinny jeans.\n\nIf you tell me your **height, weight, waist size, and whether you prefer slim/regular/loose fit**, I can narrow it down to 3 specific jeans under ₹2,000.",
